; Explain why the noun phrases did not give one object each
;
; Entered by a jump from #R$79B6 when the search for the objects of a command
; (#R$7A14) did not end with exactly one accepted object for each noun phrase.
; It prints a question or a complaint, or lets the command print its own
; refusal, and so takes the place of #R$79B6's return: the Z result with A 0
; goes back to the caller of #R$79B6 (#R$7960), which then has nothing to
; execute; the paths through #R$7DF5 go on at #R$798E, the end of that record.
; The decisions, in order:
; .
; 1. The words come from an order (InputFromOrder 1, SAY TO): return Z at once,
; silently.
; .
; 2. ALL was typed (VerbAllFlag): the objects of ALL are used up. Silently go to
; the next record (#R$7994).
; .
; 3. Exactly one accepted object for the first noun phrase (RecWork3 $7940 is
; 1): the second phrase is the trouble (#R$7D98).
; .
; 4. No words typed for the first phrase: #R$7E30.
; .
; 5. Words typed and no object or place fits them: #R$7DFE.
; .
; 6. Candidates found (RecWork2 $793F counts those that passed the check of
; the command for one object): none passed, so #R$7DF5 prints the refusal; one
; passed and a second noun is still needed, #R$7D98; one passed and the full
; check refused it, #R$7DF5; several passed, so ask "Which {word} ?" (#R$7D83).
; .
; Bits 0 and 1 of RecWork ($793D) say that the first phrase had words and that
; some object fitted them.
@label=ExplainNounFailure
c$7DBC LD A,($B71B)  ; InputFromOrder
 $7DBF DEC A         ;
 $7DC0 RET Z         ; an order: nothing is said
 $7DC1 LD A,($B71C)  ; VerbAllFlag
 $7DC4 AND A         ;
 $7DC5 JR Z,$7DCB    ;
 $7DC7 POP HL        ; ALL: drop the return address
 $7DC8 JP $7994      ; next record
*$7DCB LD A,($7940)  ; RecWork3: accepted objects for phrase 1
 $7DCE CP $01        ;
 $7DD0 JR Z,$7D98    ; ExplainNoun2Failure
 $7DD2 LD HL,$793D   ; RecWork
 $7DD5 BIT 0,(HL)    ; words typed for phrase 1?
 $7DD7 JP Z,$7E30    ; ReportNoNoun1
 $7DDA BIT 1,(HL)    ; an object fitted?
 $7DDC LD HL,$7942   ; RecBuf1
 $7DDF LD DE,$B6E8   ; FirstObject
 $7DE2 LD BC,$B6FE   ; Noun1Kind
 $7DE5 JR Z,$7DFE    ; FindNounElsewhere
 $7DE7 LD A,($793F)  ; RecWork2: candidates that passed the check
 $7DEA AND A         ;
 $7DEB JR Z,$7DF5    ; none: PerformRefusal
 $7DED DEC A         ;
 $7DEE JR NZ,$7D83   ; several: AskWhichNoun1
 $7DF0 CALL $7AD8    ; NeedSecondNoun
 $7DF3 JR NZ,$7D98   ; ExplainNoun2Failure
